## 5. NON-NEGOTIABLE SPACING & PIXEL CONTRACTS
- Keep at least 32px between the Header bottom and the first Hero copy element (24px on mobile). This spacing is over the shared background, not a separate solid band. Keep navigation visibly distinct from the Hero using its independent neutral surface.
- Use an 8px spacing rhythm: 16/24px inside cards, 32/48px between major groups, 80–112px between lower sections on desktop and 48–64px on mobile.
- Keep content in normal flow; absolute positioning is reserved for decoration inside a bounded stage. Use `min-width: 0` on grid children and avoid viewport-wide negative margins.
- Visible focus rings, 44px minimum interactive targets, semantic landmarks and heading hierarchy. Decorative layers are `aria-hidden` and `pointer-events: none`.
- At 360×800, 768×1024, 1440×900 and a short landscape viewport: no horizontal overflow, no overlapping nav/headline/CTAs; essential content stays readable.
- Check long supplied titles, empty secondary CTA, both alignment modes, keyboard navigation and 200% zoom. Reserve media dimensions to prevent layout shift.

## 6. CODE-DRIVEN MOTION CONTRACT
- Background effects span the shared Header + Hero shell (`position: relative; isolation: isolate; min-height: 100svh`) behind both navigation and copy; never constrain a background effect to a small media card. Keep product/card-specific interactions within their original foreground components. Background layers use `pointer-events: none` and never block navigation.
- Runtime: CSS radial-gradient mask + small JavaScript handler. Update --pointer-x/--pointer-y at most once per animation frame on a single background element.
- Spotlight radius 180px desktop; reveal opacity rises to .35 over 180ms on pointer enter and fades over 250ms on leave. Keep total animated area bounded to the Hero.
- Use pointer coordinates relative to the stage; do not read layout after every style write. Use one cached bounding box refreshed on resize.
- No automatic loop: stop RAF when the pointer is idle. Under coarse pointers, reduced motion or missing mask support, show a static texture at .12 opacity and attach no tracking listeners.
- Implement this effect in code; do not substitute MP4, GIF, a prerecorded animation, or a video-generation framework.
- Animate transforms and opacity where possible. Keep continuous animation outside React state updates; use requestAnimationFrame or library motion values, with effect cleanup on unmount.
- Aim for 60fps on desktop; reduce density or freeze decoration on constrained mobile devices. Pause loops when offscreen or `document.hidden`; do not run unnecessary background work.
- Do not add a visible pause/resume toolbar. Keep the template-specific looping or interaction behavior specified in this contract, respect reduced-motion preferences, and do not restart animation on ordinary re-renders.
- Under `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`, stop continuous effects and show their composed static state; keep text and CTA immediately visible. Respond to preference changes and clean up listeners.
- Primary copy must be HTML and visible before animation initialization; no loading animation may gate reading or navigation.
